  "description": "A timer the worker runs while the core is gone fires, and its end completes while a core reads the connection's control socket. The restarted core's first ping goes before its first hello, so the worker has left orphan-pending when the handshake opens; the end waits for that handshake's live and its tail goes out live. The worker then reports channel_closed by: worker with end_state, end_reason, ended_at, out_bytes, last_seq and last_out_ts as its spool entry holds them. The core records killed / idle, never terminated / target_closed, at once from the event and with no replay: a gap marker only if the event's out_bytes counts output the recording lacks (here none: the tail went out live), then the end marker and session.disconnect stamped with ended_at, then release (session-end-by-tsb steps 23a–23b).",
  "corpus": [
    "session model §11",
    "session model §12",
    "session model §15",
    "immortality §4.1",
    "immortality §4.3",
    "immortality §6.4",
    "Contract §13",
    "decision 5.45"
  ],
